\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{Matrix coefficients in the Peter–Weyl basis}
\date{2026-11-10}

\p{Choose an ordered orthonormal basis of each space #{V_\rho} in
\ref{fdip-007C}. In that basis the functions
#{\sqrt{\dim\rho}\rho(\cdot)_{ij}} form an orthonormal basis of
#{L^2(G)}. For an inequivalent exhaustive family of finite-dimensional
unitary continuous models, TauCeti's
\leanref/tauceti{TauCeti.peterWeylBasis} constructs this normalized
matrix-coefficient Hilbert basis. Over #{\mathbb C}, its coefficient
#{\langle\rho(g)e_a,e_b\rangle} is the conjugate of the matrix
entry #{\rho(g)_{ba}}; conjugation, or reindexing by dual
representations, gives the equivalent entry-coordinate basis.
The separate \leanref/tauceti{TauCeti.characterBasis} constructs
the character basis of the central #{L^2} subspace. Compact
Hausdorff groups over #{\mathbb C}, hence the compact Lie groups
of the theorem, satisfy the stated hypotheses. These correspondences
support the two #{L^2} basis statements, not the uniform absolute
convergence or the surface integral.}
